1
00:00:03,980 --> 00:00:05,580
(This program contains indirect advertisements.)

2
00:00:15,268 --> 00:00:17,368
Why don't we go to a karaoke room and get the energy up?

3
00:00:17,908 --> 00:00:19,578
Sure. Let's do it.

4
00:00:20,708 --> 00:00:23,748
(The night in Tongyeong grows deeper.)

5
00:00:23,748 --> 00:00:25,408
Why don't we sing for just one hour?

6
00:00:25,408 --> 00:00:27,478
- Okay, 1 hour would be enough.
- Seriously, just 1 hour.

7
00:00:27,478 --> 00:00:28,648
Let's have fun for an hour.

8
00:00:29,648 --> 00:00:30,648
- Oh, my.
- Hello.

9
00:00:30,648 --> 00:00:31,718
Hello.

10
00:00:32,148 --> 00:00:34,018
- We're here to sing.
- Sure.

11
00:00:34,018 --> 00:00:35,788
- Welcome.
- Hello.

12
00:00:36,658 --> 00:00:38,528
I'll give you 5 dollars. I have a 5-dollar bill.

13
00:00:38,528 --> 00:00:39,828
- You have it?
- Yes, here you go.

14
00:00:39,828 --> 00:00:41,328
You may go to Blue Crab Room.

15
00:00:41,328 --> 00:00:43,498
For Blue Crab Room, go to the side.

16
00:00:48,268 --> 00:00:50,868
This karaoke room has all kinds of things.

17
00:00:51,168 --> 00:00:55,708
(Packed with items)

18
00:00:56,348 --> 00:00:57,478
Jung Ah, do you want a matching set with me?

19
00:00:57,478 --> 00:00:59,878
- That way, we can sing together.
- Yes.

20
00:00:59,878 --> 00:01:01,318
- I'll go later.
- Really?

21
00:01:01,318 --> 00:01:03,388
(Giant bow sisters)

22
00:01:03,388 --> 00:01:04,588
That looks cute.

23
00:01:04,588 --> 00:01:05,618
(Each of them puts on one item.)

24
00:01:05,618 --> 00:01:07,288
- Keep it more to the front.
- Okay.

25
00:01:07,958 --> 00:01:09,518
- Thank you.
- Let's go to Blue Crab Room.

26
00:01:09,518 --> 00:01:10,628
(Heading to Blue Crab Room)

27
00:01:11,358 --> 00:01:13,258
Press the start button.

28
00:01:13,828 --> 00:01:15,158
- Are you going to start?
- Press start.

29
00:01:15,158 --> 00:01:16,368
- Okay.
- I will...

30
00:01:16,868 --> 00:01:18,998
It's a little embarrassing to sing in front of you.

31
00:01:19,198 --> 00:01:23,438
(He felt a lot of pressure for his karaoke debut.)

32
00:01:23,738 --> 00:01:24,938
(Will he be able to pull it off?)

33
00:01:24,938 --> 00:01:26,578
I will start.

34
00:01:26,808 --> 00:01:29,178
I don't usually go to karaoke bars.

35
00:01:30,478 --> 00:01:32,778
Since I'm in front of you, I'll put on a little show.

36
00:01:33,418 --> 00:01:35,718
(Let's start You Soon's talent show.)

37
00:01:37,388 --> 00:01:39,018
When I happened to see you

38
00:01:39,448 --> 00:01:42,318
(A sudden change)

39
00:01:42,658 --> 00:01:46,058
(Why did he even worry?)

40
00:01:46,458 --> 00:01:50,198
Those eyes of yours

41
00:01:50,828 --> 00:01:53,368
(They're captivated right away.)

42
00:01:53,498 --> 00:01:57,938
(There's something I want to tell you)

43
00:01:58,238 --> 00:02:01,438
(Puppy Kang is also good at singing.)

44
00:02:01,538 --> 00:02:04,078
(Feeling proud of him)

45
00:02:04,248 --> 00:02:05,848
(Boom, clap)

46
00:02:06,248 --> 00:02:07,248
(Exclaiming)

47
00:02:08,048 --> 00:02:10,618
(Taking over the stage)

48
00:02:10,948 --> 00:02:13,518
(The youngest is also having a blast.)

49
00:02:13,788 --> 00:02:17,228
(Fool)

50
00:02:17,658 --> 00:02:19,698
(I must be a fool)

51
00:02:21,128 --> 00:02:23,598
(Dance time, let's go!)

52
00:02:23,998 --> 00:02:25,868
(Step to the left, step to the right)

53
00:02:26,028 --> 00:02:27,798
(Wiggling)

54
00:02:28,298 --> 00:02:29,298
Oh, my.

55
00:02:29,708 --> 00:02:32,038
This is what he was setting us up for.

56
00:02:32,038 --> 00:02:34,408
- I hardly ever sing.
- He said that he was a bad singer.

57
00:02:34,708 --> 00:02:37,448
(Why did I say that?)

58
00:02:37,448 --> 00:02:38,478
Look at him.

59
00:02:38,478 --> 00:02:39,548
(He was born to be a karaoke star.)

60
00:02:39,548 --> 00:02:40,578
My gosh.

61
00:02:41,918 --> 00:02:44,718
(You Seok's debut performance is a huge success.)

62
00:02:44,718 --> 00:02:46,688
- That was insane.
- Seriously...

63
00:02:46,688 --> 00:02:48,018
That was cute.

64
00:02:48,618 --> 00:02:50,158
- That was insane.
- I don't sing just anywhere.

65
00:02:50,158 --> 00:02:51,658
By the way...

66
00:02:51,658 --> 00:02:52,658
Gosh.

67
00:02:52,658 --> 00:02:54,498
- The headband looks great on you.
- I agree.

68
00:02:54,498 --> 00:02:56,568
It looks perfect on you.

69
00:02:57,328 --> 00:02:59,398
- "A Flower Yet to Bloom?" - The youngest is good.

70
00:03:00,438 --> 00:03:02,638
- "A Flower Yet to Bloom?" - The youngest is good.

71
00:03:02,638 --> 00:03:04,238
It's been over ten years...

72
00:03:05,208 --> 00:03:07,608
since I last came to karaoke.

73
00:03:07,608 --> 00:03:09,078
- That's great.
- It's been over ten years.

74
00:03:09,608 --> 00:03:11,808
(Shyly making his way onto the stage)

75
00:03:12,548 --> 00:03:14,578
Are you not coming?

76
00:03:15,418 --> 00:03:18,488
(His voice is great,)

77
00:03:18,488 --> 00:03:21,618
(and the vibes are good.)

78
00:03:23,788 --> 00:03:26,498
(Casually)

79
00:03:27,328 --> 00:03:30,328
(Slipping his hand in his pocket)

80
00:03:30,328 --> 00:03:33,798
(Packing every ounce of middle-aged emotion into the performance)

81
00:03:34,168 --> 00:03:39,538
(Upon a bare, lonely branch)

82
00:03:40,438 --> 00:03:44,078
(His deeply emotional voice has everyone tearing up.)

83
00:03:44,078 --> 00:03:45,178
(Jingling)

84
00:03:46,148 --> 00:03:51,148
(Alone, trying to make a single flower bloom)

85
00:03:51,518 --> 00:03:57,358
(Are you trembling in sorrow?)

86
00:03:57,728 --> 00:04:00,828
(Even the bird that cried along with you grows weary)

87
00:04:00,828 --> 00:04:03,628
(Exploding with emotions)

88
00:04:04,898 --> 00:04:09,338
(He definitely has a story.)

89
00:04:09,738 --> 00:04:13,278
(At his anguished cry,)

90
00:04:13,278 --> 00:04:15,908
(the audience is also getting teary.)

91
00:04:16,648 --> 00:04:24,588
(I'll make that one unbloomed flower finally bloom)

92
00:04:26,248 --> 00:04:29,118
(Giving it everything for the finale)

93
00:04:29,388 --> 00:04:31,628
- He's a good singer.
- He's good.

94
00:04:31,728 --> 00:04:32,928
- He's very good at singing.
- You're amazing.

95
00:04:32,928 --> 00:04:33,998
(He destroyed that stage.)

96
00:04:33,998 --> 00:04:36,128
(The lingering afterglow)

97
00:04:36,598 --> 00:04:40,238
(It's time to shake things up after the ballad song.)

98
00:04:40,738 --> 00:04:42,898
(Following the entertainment director, Yoon Seo)

99
00:04:42,898 --> 00:04:45,738
(Raise the energy!)

100
00:04:46,508 --> 00:04:49,978
(Because I'm a cruel woman)

101
00:04:53,248 --> 00:04:55,848
(Screaming)

102
00:04:56,278 --> 00:04:59,918
(The art student is killing it.)

103
00:05:00,658 --> 00:05:04,358
(Forever)

104
00:05:04,688 --> 00:05:06,798
(This is her ending pose.)

105
00:05:06,798 --> 00:05:07,798
Well done.

106
00:05:08,058 --> 00:05:10,128
(Our youngest is doing well.)

107
00:05:10,868 --> 00:05:14,468
(Throwing in "TTL" since she's good)

108
00:05:15,038 --> 00:05:17,638
(She's not swimming.)

109
00:05:18,238 --> 00:05:21,878
(The youngest can rap too.)

110
00:05:26,408 --> 00:05:29,218
(In case I see you, in case you come back)

111
00:05:29,778 --> 00:05:31,988
(After finishing the 1st verse with a bang)

112
00:05:31,988 --> 00:05:33,018
Cancel it.

113
00:05:34,988 --> 00:05:36,088
- I still love you...
- Oh, my.

114
00:05:36,088 --> 00:05:37,158
(I still love you)

115
00:05:37,558 --> 00:05:40,828
(The song stops.)

116
00:05:41,358 --> 00:05:43,268
(Embarrassed)

117
00:05:43,268 --> 00:05:45,198
(I'm so sorry.)

118
00:05:45,598 --> 00:05:47,768
I guess the song is over

119
00:05:48,998 --> 00:05:52,538
(Feeling awkward)

120
00:05:53,008 --> 00:05:54,008
I must be flustered

121
00:05:54,008 --> 00:05:57,148
(Who is this man?)

122
00:05:57,408 --> 00:06:00,178
How can our timing be this bad?

123
00:06:02,118 --> 00:06:04,248
I guess we're not meant to be

124
00:06:06,018 --> 00:06:08,988
(Let's enjoy a little more of the youngest ones' talent show)

125
00:06:09,258 --> 00:06:12,358
(Yoon Seo is filming him.)

126
00:06:12,428 --> 00:06:13,498
(Yoon Seo's camera)

127
00:06:13,498 --> 00:06:17,828
(Nostalgic)

128
00:06:18,598 --> 00:06:21,968
(Yoon Seo is being filmed this time.)

129
00:06:22,068 --> 00:06:23,708
(Hae Joon's camera)

130
00:06:23,708 --> 00:06:28,778
(Here we have a coming-of-age movie.)

131
00:06:30,508 --> 00:06:33,478
(Peekaboo)

132
00:06:34,078 --> 00:06:37,018
(The siblings have a wonderful time.)

133
00:06:37,588 --> 00:06:42,818
(They even sang along to AKMU songs they had been singing all day.)

134
00:06:43,458 --> 00:06:46,058
(On cloudy days)

135
00:06:46,058 --> 00:06:49,258
(On sunny days)

136
00:06:50,068 --> 00:06:51,698
I think I lost my voice from singing.

137
00:06:52,098 --> 00:06:54,498
- That was so much fun.
- We really made the most...

138
00:06:54,498 --> 00:06:57,038
- of our day.
- The day was very long.

139
00:06:57,038 --> 00:06:59,008
(With a promise to keep having fun, they wrap up the day.)

140
00:06:59,268 --> 00:07:00,678
Hae Joon is...

141
00:07:01,338 --> 00:07:02,778
quite special.

142
00:07:03,408 --> 00:07:04,448
You met him for the first time, but don't you feel...

143
00:07:04,448 --> 00:07:05,478
- comfortable around him?
- I do.

144
00:07:05,478 --> 00:07:07,048
- Isn't it strangely comfortable?
- Exactly.

145
00:07:07,048 --> 00:07:08,218
- Isn't it strange?
- Yes.

146
00:07:08,718 --> 00:07:09,748
I'm so glad that you're here.

147
00:07:11,518 --> 00:07:12,888
For you,

148
00:07:13,018 --> 00:07:15,388
I'd come anytime.

149
00:07:16,658 --> 00:07:19,688
The three of us were in "Love, Take Two."

150
00:07:19,688 --> 00:07:21,058
(They co-starred in "Love, Take Two.")

151
00:07:21,058 --> 00:07:22,658
- You played You Seok's dad.
- Right.

152
00:07:22,998 --> 00:07:24,028
It'd be strange...

153
00:07:24,028 --> 00:07:25,028
- if you hadn't come.
- Right.

154
00:07:25,028 --> 00:07:26,098
(It was impossible for him not to come.)

155
00:07:26,098 --> 00:07:28,198
If Jung Ah asked anyone...

156
00:07:28,598 --> 00:07:31,638
to come, they'd all come.

157
00:07:32,038 --> 00:07:33,038
- It's quite amazing.
- Yes.

158
00:07:33,038 --> 00:07:34,778
- You mean, Jung Ah?
- Yes.

159
00:07:34,778 --> 00:07:35,908
(That's the charm of Captain Yum.)

160
00:07:35,908 --> 00:07:39,148
When I was invited to this show,

161
00:07:39,148 --> 00:07:41,748
- I also came here for Jung Ah.
- I said yes without looking back.

162
00:07:44,048 --> 00:07:45,548
- It was because of Jung Ah.
- I came here because of you.

163
00:07:46,958 --> 00:07:49,358
- But it's over.
- Right, I came here for you too.

164
00:07:49,588 --> 00:07:50,588
I had never seen you, but...

165
00:07:50,588 --> 00:07:52,358
- Right, I came here for you too.
- But it's over.

166
00:07:52,358 --> 00:07:54,098
I had never seen you, but...

167
00:07:54,198 --> 00:07:55,928
You're right. I almost forgot.

168
00:07:56,358 --> 00:07:57,598
Jung Ah wasn't that important.

169
00:07:58,498 --> 00:08:01,098
- I came here for You Seok.
- Me too.

170
00:08:01,368 --> 00:08:04,038
I came here for You Seok. When I found out about him,

171
00:08:04,038 --> 00:08:06,068
I said, "I'll definitely go."

172
00:08:07,138 --> 00:08:08,978
(Just then, Captain Yum comes back.)

173
00:08:09,408 --> 00:08:11,408
- It's not about catching something.
- We'll catch flatfish.

174
00:08:11,808 --> 00:08:13,208
- It's just a ride.
- It's a ride.

175
00:08:13,718 --> 00:08:15,718
It's for You Seok to have fun.

176
00:08:15,878 --> 00:08:18,488
- No.
- Can't we ride the boat at 10am?

177
00:08:18,488 --> 00:08:20,958
I don't need to ride it again. I already did it.

178
00:08:20,958 --> 00:08:22,858
Then why are you sticking out your lips?

179
00:08:22,858 --> 00:08:24,328
We already rode the boat. This time...

180
00:08:24,328 --> 00:08:26,228
But you keep sticking out your lower lip.

181
00:08:26,228 --> 00:08:28,898
- Why does it keep sticking out?
- That's not true.

182
00:08:29,058 --> 00:08:30,068
I'm serious this time.

183
00:08:30,068 --> 00:08:32,498
I saw him from a 90° angle.

184
00:08:32,498 --> 00:08:35,038
- You Seok does everything he wants.
- No way.

185
00:08:35,898 --> 00:08:38,908
- His cuteness as his weapon.
- But I love it.

186
00:08:38,908 --> 00:08:41,878
I love that you all let me do whatever I want.

187
00:08:43,508 --> 00:08:45,808
This isn't a place where...

188
00:08:45,808 --> 00:08:47,578
you get to check off your bucket list.

189
00:08:47,848 --> 00:08:50,588
I did everything. I went luge riding, and I drove a boat.

190
00:08:50,888 --> 00:08:51,888
I accomplished everything on my list.

191
00:08:52,248 --> 00:08:55,488
The last one up is Kang You Seok.

192
00:08:55,488 --> 00:08:56,518
I don't want to wash up.

193
00:08:56,588 --> 00:08:59,228
- You Seok, dry your hair.
- I never dry my hair.

194
00:09:01,398 --> 00:09:02,398
- That's cool.
- Jung Ah.

195
00:09:03,128 --> 00:09:05,028
Why don't you tell me to dry my hair?

196
00:09:05,328 --> 00:09:07,968
- You haven't dried your hair?
- I tied it up right away.

197
00:09:07,968 --> 00:09:10,368
- Don't tie it up while it's wet.
- You shouldn't do that.

198
00:09:10,668 --> 00:09:12,438
He and I are the same.

199
00:09:12,438 --> 00:09:14,638
- No, you should dry your hair.
- Sun Young.

200
00:09:14,638 --> 00:09:16,878
- Why not?
- What's wrong with him?

201
00:09:16,878 --> 00:09:18,648
Your hair isn't as long as hers.

202
00:09:18,648 --> 00:09:20,178
Your hair is short. Why is it not okay?

203
00:09:20,578 --> 00:09:22,918
It's definitely not okay. You need to dry your scalp first.

204
00:09:22,918 --> 00:09:24,548
It's bad for your hair and scalp.

205
00:09:24,548 --> 00:09:25,548
It's bad for your scalp.

206
00:09:27,788 --> 00:09:28,958
This is for sure.

207
00:09:29,218 --> 00:09:30,458
(They're two peas in a pod.)

208
00:09:30,458 --> 00:09:31,528
My goodness.

209
00:09:32,458 --> 00:09:33,498
Let's go to bed.

210
00:09:33,498 --> 00:09:34,728
- We should.
- Let's sleep.

211
00:09:35,028 --> 00:09:37,228
We need sleep for tomorrow.

212
00:09:38,128 --> 00:09:39,228
Sleep well.

213
00:09:39,628 --> 00:09:41,598
- Good night.
- Sleep well.

214
00:09:43,038 --> 00:09:48,578
(As the hiding sun slowly peeks its head out)

215
00:09:49,778 --> 00:09:52,478
(Morning arrives in Sopo Village.)

216
00:09:53,478 --> 00:09:58,788
(Some already started their day early.)

217
00:09:59,948 --> 00:10:02,218
(Cats...)

218
00:10:02,218 --> 00:10:05,028
(and magpies welcome the morning in their own ways.)

219
00:10:06,188 --> 00:10:08,398
(It's time for the siblings to wake up.)

220
00:10:09,928 --> 00:10:11,828
(But the house is completely quiet.)

221
00:10:13,098 --> 00:10:16,038
(They had promised to take the outboard boat at 7am.)

222
00:10:17,238 --> 00:10:19,738
(Yet there's no sign of the two of them getting up.)

223
00:10:21,008 --> 00:10:25,808
(Just then, Jung Ah gets up.)

224
00:10:29,748 --> 00:10:32,988
(Did the boys leave?)

225
00:10:33,458 --> 00:10:34,818
(Knocking)

226
00:10:37,628 --> 00:10:38,728
Gosh, they're still here.

227
00:10:39,188 --> 00:10:41,058
- What?
- Aren't you going to work out?

228
00:10:41,858 --> 00:10:43,698
- Work out?
- Aren't you going on the boat?

229
00:10:44,598 --> 00:10:46,168
- You Seok.
- Hey.

230
00:10:46,168 --> 00:10:47,898
(She wakes up You Seok who's still sleeping.)

231
00:10:47,898 --> 00:10:48,898
My goodness.

232
00:10:50,098 --> 00:10:51,208
They aren't up yet.

233
00:10:51,668 --> 00:10:52,708
I guess they slept through.

234
00:10:52,708 --> 00:10:55,078
They were supposed to leave at 7am, but they're still in bed.

235
00:10:56,578 --> 00:11:00,648
(She goes right back to dreamland.)

236
00:11:01,048 --> 00:11:02,318
(The two of them are still half asleep.)

237
00:11:02,318 --> 00:11:04,048
I'll take a shower when we get back.

238
00:11:05,748 --> 00:11:07,758
(While Hae Joon goes to shower first,)

239
00:11:08,558 --> 00:11:11,328
(You Seok gets up.)

240
00:11:12,088 --> 00:11:15,628
(Opening up the curtains)

241
00:11:17,568 --> 00:11:20,538
(He even neatly makes the bed.)

242
00:11:21,468 --> 00:11:24,468
(After washing up, he puts on sunscreen.)

243
00:11:25,108 --> 00:11:26,538
- Let's go.
- Let's go.

244
00:11:26,538 --> 00:11:27,578
(They're ready to head out.)

245
00:11:27,838 --> 00:11:29,338
Are you taking your jacket with you?

246
00:11:29,778 --> 00:11:32,248
- It's cold when you're at the sea.
- No, it's not.

247
00:11:32,248 --> 00:11:34,848
- Goodness.
- It's not cold. I'm serious.

248
00:11:34,848 --> 00:11:36,518
(They start bickering from the moment they leave.)

249
00:11:36,718 --> 00:11:38,548
How much fun could riding a boat be?

250
00:11:39,688 --> 00:11:41,158
I want to give you a boat ride.

251
00:11:41,158 --> 00:11:42,618
You've only been on a boat with my older sister.

252
00:11:42,618 --> 00:11:44,088
(In the drama, Hae Joon only went on a boat with his daughter.)

253
00:11:44,988 --> 00:11:47,158
Were you disappointed by that?

254
00:11:47,158 --> 00:11:48,228
(He doesn't deny it.)

255
00:11:48,228 --> 00:11:49,228
Eun Myeong.

256
00:11:49,998 --> 00:11:52,098
- Yes, Father.
- Don't be disappointed.

257
00:11:52,098 --> 00:11:53,398
(Simple)

258
00:11:54,238 --> 00:11:55,838
Gosh, the water is clear.

259
00:11:56,538 --> 00:11:58,038
- What?
- The water is clear.

260
00:11:58,038 --> 00:11:59,308
Yes, it's very clear.

261
00:11:59,908 --> 00:12:02,208
How can the seawater be this clear?

262
00:12:02,308 --> 00:12:03,378
(It's so clear you can see all the way to the bottom.)

263
00:12:04,108 --> 00:12:06,608
(There are also winkles living here.)

264
00:12:07,578 --> 00:12:09,878
(With excitement, they head out to get on the boat.)

265
00:12:10,818 --> 00:12:12,448
(Buckling their seat belts)

266
00:12:12,448 --> 00:12:13,448
Did you put on your seat belt?

267
00:12:14,318 --> 00:12:15,818
- Here we go.
- Yes, let's go.

268
00:12:17,388 --> 00:12:18,788
Let's go.

269
00:12:21,628 --> 00:12:23,868
The weather is beautiful. Even the smell...

270
00:12:23,868 --> 00:12:25,628
(Under the sunlight that sparkles even more brightly today,)

271
00:12:25,628 --> 00:12:30,868
(the peaceful scenery passes by outside the window.)

272
00:12:32,168 --> 00:12:35,678
(Father and son happily set off on a little date of their own.)

273
00:12:36,308 --> 00:12:39,978
So this is what it feels like to have your son drive you around.

274
00:12:40,748 --> 00:12:41,948
It's touching.

275
00:12:41,948 --> 00:12:44,188
(Watching his son drive somehow brings a lump to his throat.)

276
00:12:44,188 --> 00:12:46,918
When did he become an adult?

277
00:12:46,918 --> 00:12:48,018
(When did my son grow up so much?)

278
00:12:48,418 --> 00:12:49,518
This is great.

279
00:12:49,518 --> 00:12:50,728
(I'm loving this moment.)

280
00:12:50,858 --> 00:12:53,188
He's driving for me and taking me out on the boat.

281
00:12:53,658 --> 00:12:55,098
- I'll take you everywhere.
- Yes.

282
00:12:55,098 --> 00:12:56,198
(His son is giving up the full treatment.)

283
00:12:56,358 --> 00:12:57,828
You've done your duty as a good son.

284
00:12:57,828 --> 00:13:00,168
(Smiling)

285
00:13:01,098 --> 00:13:03,808
(As they continue down the road,)

286
00:13:03,808 --> 00:13:07,008
(the blue sea comes into view on the right.)

287
00:13:07,908 --> 00:13:08,978
My goodness.

288
00:13:08,978 --> 00:13:10,448
(Staring)

289
00:13:10,508 --> 00:13:12,778
How is the water so clear? It's the sea.

290
00:13:13,778 --> 00:13:14,918
It's fascinating.

291
00:13:14,918 --> 00:13:16,818
(Now matter how many times you look,)

292
00:13:16,818 --> 00:13:18,748
(the clear ocean is breathtaking.)

293
00:13:19,418 --> 00:13:20,518
(They can't stop marvelling at it.)

294
00:13:20,518 --> 00:13:22,518
- Isn't it beautiful?
- The view is magnificent.

295
00:13:24,288 --> 00:13:29,158
(After taking in the brilliant blue sea and deep green landscape)

296
00:13:29,358 --> 00:13:30,528
We're here.

297
00:13:30,598 --> 00:13:32,998
(They finally arrive at the outboard boat dock.)

298
00:13:32,998 --> 00:13:34,268
- Are we here?
- Yes.

299
00:13:35,138 --> 00:13:36,338
"Water sports place?"

300
00:13:36,638 --> 00:13:38,938
- This is...
- We can get out.

301
00:13:38,938 --> 00:13:40,878
(I'll guide you once you get out.)

302
00:13:41,078 --> 00:13:42,208
Hello.

303
00:13:42,208 --> 00:13:43,778
Did you enjoy it last time?

304
00:13:44,348 --> 00:13:45,878
I came back with my father this time.

305
00:13:45,878 --> 00:13:47,618
- I see.
- Your father?

306
00:13:49,518 --> 00:13:53,788
(They put on their life jackets and fasten the strap.)

307
00:13:54,158 --> 00:13:56,018
- Do you want to fish?
- Sure.

308
00:13:56,288 --> 00:13:57,288
- You want to?
- Yes.

309
00:13:57,288 --> 00:13:58,388
(Today, they're also planning to go fishing.)

310
00:13:58,388 --> 00:14:01,628
(As these outboard boats are easy to operate without a boating license,)

311
00:14:02,228 --> 00:14:04,728
(many people drive them out to their preferred fishing spots...)

312
00:14:05,268 --> 00:14:09,168
(and enjoy fishing from that boat.)

313
00:14:09,498 --> 00:14:10,608
Do you know how to fish?

314
00:14:11,808 --> 00:14:13,778
You just cast it.

315
00:14:13,778 --> 00:14:14,878
(Fishing is just casting.)

316
00:14:15,638 --> 00:14:17,548
(He boards the boat with confident steps.)

317
00:14:17,548 --> 00:14:18,648
Hey, this is...

318
00:14:18,648 --> 00:14:20,248
(Being careful)

319
00:14:20,248 --> 00:14:21,348
Once we go...

320
00:14:22,118 --> 00:14:23,848
- Do you want to operate it?
- No.

321
00:14:24,618 --> 00:14:27,058
Operating it is easier than you think.

322
00:14:27,118 --> 00:14:28,118
Are you...

323
00:14:28,118 --> 00:14:29,518
(Fully at ease on his 2nd time on an outboard boat)

324
00:14:29,618 --> 00:14:31,158
- Shall we set out now?
- Are you...

325
00:14:31,258 --> 00:14:32,588
going to operate it?

326
00:14:32,588 --> 00:14:33,898
It'll just be the two of us.

327
00:14:33,898 --> 00:14:35,798
- Seriously?
- Yes.

328
00:14:36,358 --> 00:14:37,928
This is great.

329
00:14:37,928 --> 00:14:39,028
Captain.

330
00:14:39,728 --> 00:14:40,738
Let's go.

331
00:14:43,338 --> 00:14:46,468
(I'll make sure you're taken care of.)

332
00:14:48,478 --> 00:14:51,848
(Captain Kang is getting more skilled at driving it.)

333
00:14:52,848 --> 00:14:54,118
Let's go.

334
00:14:54,648 --> 00:14:57,488
Father, let's go and catch some fish.

335
00:15:00,248 --> 00:15:04,428
(They set off with dreams of returning with a boat full of fish.)

336
00:15:06,858 --> 00:15:07,898
(Exclaiming)

337
00:15:09,398 --> 00:15:11,998
I didn't think you'd operate the boat.

338
00:15:12,298 --> 00:15:14,438
- You didn't know?
- No.

339
00:15:14,638 --> 00:15:17,308
You thought that someone else would drive it?

340
00:15:18,238 --> 00:15:19,908
That's not fun.

341
00:15:21,908 --> 00:15:23,438
Gosh, this is great.

342
00:15:23,438 --> 00:15:26,878
(Having You Seok drive makes it even more fun.)

343
00:15:27,778 --> 00:15:28,848
All right.

344
00:15:30,448 --> 00:15:31,488
Gosh, this is good.

345
00:15:31,488 --> 00:15:34,058
(They power through the deep blue sea.)

346
00:15:34,988 --> 00:15:36,358
The water is very calm.

347
00:15:36,358 --> 00:15:37,988
(As they take in the scenery around them)

348
00:15:38,388 --> 00:15:42,128
Shall we fish over here?

349
00:15:42,728 --> 00:15:44,298
- Is this a fishing spot?
- Yes.

350
00:15:45,568 --> 00:15:46,598
Do you know how to fish?

351
00:15:47,538 --> 00:15:49,768
Don't you just throw it in...

352
00:15:49,768 --> 00:15:50,808
(Full of confidence)

353
00:15:50,808 --> 00:15:52,608
And catch fish?

354
00:15:54,038 --> 00:15:56,038
(They both try putting some bait on their hooks.)

355
00:15:56,838 --> 00:15:57,948
(Glancing)

356
00:15:57,948 --> 00:15:59,908
(A long, dangling earthworm)

357
00:16:00,308 --> 00:16:01,478
You've never been fishing before, have you?

358
00:16:02,018 --> 00:16:03,748
- What?
- You can't hook it on like that.

359
00:16:03,988 --> 00:16:06,518
- You think so, right?
- Yes.

360
00:16:06,518 --> 00:16:07,718
You've never been fishing, have you?

361
00:16:08,088 --> 00:16:09,258
(Goodness)

362
00:16:09,488 --> 00:16:11,058
It shouldn't be too short.

363
00:16:11,058 --> 00:16:13,458
Fish will bite it off and leave.

364
00:16:15,028 --> 00:16:17,058
(This won't work, You Seok.)

365
00:16:17,698 --> 00:16:20,968
(I'll show you what fishing is about.)

366
00:16:21,738 --> 00:16:24,138
(He's throwing it.)

367
00:16:26,808 --> 00:16:28,208
(What?)

368
00:16:29,578 --> 00:16:32,648
(The fishing line comes loose before he gets a proper casting.)

369
00:16:33,608 --> 00:16:35,918
(Flustered)

370
00:16:36,978 --> 00:16:37,988
This is...

371
00:16:39,048 --> 00:16:40,218
Gosh.

372
00:16:40,218 --> 00:16:41,588
(Shooing off)

373
00:16:42,218 --> 00:16:43,358
Gosh.

374
00:16:43,618 --> 00:16:45,428
(It looks like it landed somewhere up ahead.)

375
00:16:46,688 --> 00:16:48,958
- How do I undo it?
- That...

376
00:16:50,158 --> 00:16:51,168
(The bait goes in and comes right back out.)

377
00:16:51,168 --> 00:16:52,528
Let me see.

378
00:16:53,198 --> 00:16:55,538
(Their first casts end in anticlimactic failure.)

379
00:16:55,868 --> 00:16:58,838
Aren't we supposed to cast it way out there?

380
00:16:59,138 --> 00:17:01,008
But we're only beginners.

381
00:17:01,008 --> 00:17:02,378
(Being very honest)

382
00:17:02,438 --> 00:17:05,248
It'd be nice to catch some fish.

383
00:17:06,748 --> 00:17:11,118
(It's a big dream for beginners.)

384
00:17:13,548 --> 00:17:14,558
There's no fish.

385
00:17:15,858 --> 00:17:17,988
You haven't waited long enough.

386
00:17:19,028 --> 00:17:20,598
Aren't you supposed to catch it fast?

387
00:17:20,598 --> 00:17:21,828
Of course not.

388
00:17:23,728 --> 00:17:25,828
Is this a spot without fish?

389
00:17:25,828 --> 00:17:27,598
(In 2 minutes, he already gets impatient.)

390
00:17:27,598 --> 00:17:28,698
Just wait.

391
00:17:29,398 --> 00:17:30,838
It isn't as easy as you think.

392
00:17:30,838 --> 00:17:33,508
Should we get closer to that island?

393
00:17:33,938 --> 00:17:35,738
You cast it not so long ago.

394
00:17:35,738 --> 00:17:38,478
(Fishing is all about staying in your seat.)

395
00:17:38,478 --> 00:17:40,408
(Getting up)

396
00:17:41,278 --> 00:17:44,888
(Yet he moves immediately to another spot.)

397
00:17:44,888 --> 00:17:47,048
(Moving again)

398
00:17:47,048 --> 00:17:48,288
(Moving three times)

399
00:17:48,288 --> 00:17:49,358
Goodness.

400
00:17:50,258 --> 00:17:52,628
(His butt isn't heavy enough.)

401
00:17:52,628 --> 00:17:54,228
I don't think we'll catch any.

402
00:17:55,558 --> 00:17:57,498
I was worried that we'd catch too much.

403
00:17:57,498 --> 00:17:59,428
- What? Seriously?
- What if we catch too much?

404
00:17:59,898 --> 00:18:02,468
Fishing isn't as easy as I thought.

405
00:18:03,938 --> 00:18:06,138
(Meanwhile, at home,)

406
00:18:06,768 --> 00:18:08,578
(the youngest is up and getting ready.)

407
00:18:09,578 --> 00:18:10,678
(Grunting)

408
00:18:11,608 --> 00:18:13,208
They went for a boat ride.

409
00:18:13,208 --> 00:18:14,518
(Laughing)

410
00:18:14,878 --> 00:18:17,588
The two of them are hilarious.

411
00:18:17,588 --> 00:18:19,418
(The whole situation is just too funny.)

412
00:18:19,418 --> 00:18:20,618
They're going to fish.

413
00:18:20,918 --> 00:18:22,288
On that boat?

414
00:18:23,488 --> 00:18:25,358
Who goes fishing on that boat?

415
00:18:25,358 --> 00:18:26,388
It's impossible.

416
00:18:26,388 --> 00:18:28,428
(We do.)

417
00:18:28,798 --> 00:18:31,268
(Putting their worries aside, they laugh at the thought of them.)

418
00:18:31,868 --> 00:18:34,368
(Shall we start the day?)

419
00:18:34,738 --> 00:18:36,568
It's time to get up.

420
00:18:36,568 --> 00:18:37,608
Okay.

421
00:18:39,038 --> 00:18:40,068
(Still half asleep, she staggers off to wash up.)

422
00:18:40,068 --> 00:18:41,178
What's this?

423
00:18:41,778 --> 00:18:43,978
I should've started the washing machine.

424
00:18:44,848 --> 00:18:46,978
(The morning officially begins.)

425
00:18:48,218 --> 00:18:49,478
(Whoosh)

426
00:18:50,218 --> 00:18:51,488
Goodness.

427
00:18:51,488 --> 00:18:52,888
(The youngest immediately starts making the bed.)

428
00:18:53,418 --> 00:18:55,258
You're doing well.

429
00:18:55,318 --> 00:18:57,928
- I'm doing well.
- You're doing well.

430
00:18:59,558 --> 00:19:01,858
(Encouraged by Jung Ah's praise, she picks up the pace.)

431
00:19:01,858 --> 00:19:03,028
All right.

432
00:19:03,898 --> 00:19:04,898
There we go.

433
00:19:04,898 --> 00:19:05,898
(The bed is made in no time.)

434
00:19:06,398 --> 00:19:08,138
(Surprised)

435
00:19:08,338 --> 00:19:11,138
- Thank you.
- Yoon Seo did it all.

436
00:19:11,138 --> 00:19:12,968
(Smiling at the youngest's sweet little gesture)

437
00:19:16,508 --> 00:19:18,478
(Hae Joon and You Seok still haven't caught a single fish.)

438
00:19:18,548 --> 00:19:20,178
I guess there's no fish here.

439
00:19:20,978 --> 00:19:22,918
- There's no fish here.
- What?

440
00:19:22,918 --> 00:19:24,018
There's no fish here.

441
00:19:24,718 --> 00:19:26,688
- Shall we go, father?
- Let's go.

442
00:19:26,688 --> 00:19:27,688
(After 30 minutes, they give up fishing.)

443
00:19:27,688 --> 00:19:28,718
Where should I hang it?

444
00:19:28,888 --> 00:19:30,758
We should've caught one.

445
00:19:30,758 --> 00:19:31,988
It's impossible.

446
00:19:32,288 --> 00:19:33,828
- I'll turn the boat around.
- Let's go.

447
00:19:33,828 --> 00:19:35,298
(Let's go back home.)

448
00:19:35,628 --> 00:19:37,598
Gosh, the weather is beautiful.

449
00:19:39,328 --> 00:19:40,968
- Father.
- Yes?

450
00:19:41,438 --> 00:19:42,468
Are you liking it?

451
00:19:43,138 --> 00:19:44,238
Keep going straight.

452
00:19:46,308 --> 00:19:47,678
This is great.

453
00:19:47,678 --> 00:19:49,508
(They may have caught nothing, but they're still positive.)

454
00:19:52,678 --> 00:19:54,878
Can't we take this boat...

455
00:19:55,548 --> 00:19:58,588
all the way to the port in front of our house?

456
00:19:58,588 --> 00:19:59,948
- I see.
- All the way to our house.

457
00:20:00,018 --> 00:20:01,618
The sea must be connected.

458
00:20:01,618 --> 00:20:02,658
Of course it is.

459
00:20:03,218 --> 00:20:05,258
Shall we give it a go?

460
00:20:05,358 --> 00:20:06,988
(The outboard boat can only be operated in designated areas.)

461
00:20:07,458 --> 00:20:08,758
The boat ride is a lot of fun.

462
00:20:08,858 --> 00:20:09,928
Right?

463
00:20:10,298 --> 00:20:11,398
Aren't you glad that you came?

464
00:20:11,568 --> 00:20:12,568
I like it.

465
00:20:12,568 --> 00:20:13,568
(A memorable date for the two of them)

466
00:20:14,068 --> 00:20:15,868
What shall we have for breakfast?

467
00:20:16,638 --> 00:20:19,338
We'll make seaweed pot rice with seaweed we got yesterday.

468
00:20:19,338 --> 00:20:20,978
I've never made pot rice before,

469
00:20:21,208 --> 00:20:22,378
so there's a chance that I mess it up.

470
00:20:22,378 --> 00:20:24,108
Jung Ah, it will still be delicious.

471
00:20:24,108 --> 00:20:25,108
(What Jung Ah makes is guaranteed to be good.)

472
00:20:25,108 --> 00:20:27,148
Just in case I mess it up,

473
00:20:27,148 --> 00:20:29,218
I'll also make delicious green onion yukgaejang.

474
00:20:29,218 --> 00:20:30,218
(Breakfast item 2: Green onion yukgaejang)

475
00:20:30,218 --> 00:20:31,218
This way.

476
00:20:31,218 --> 00:20:33,018
(From the vast Geoje sea in the southern coast)

477
00:20:33,888 --> 00:20:38,428
(They painstakingly hauled up with a 9.3-meter pulling rake.)

478
00:20:39,588 --> 00:20:42,798
(Gyeonnaeryang’s seasonal specialty, wild rock seaweed)

479
00:20:43,658 --> 00:20:46,798
(How about making breakfast with this precious wild seaweed?)

480
00:20:47,468 --> 00:20:48,598
We need...

481
00:20:48,598 --> 00:20:50,268
to set up two burners.

482
00:20:50,268 --> 00:20:51,638
- The fire? Okay.
- You know...

483
00:20:53,068 --> 00:20:54,578
(The youngest is in charge of fire today instead of You Seok.)

484
00:20:54,578 --> 00:20:57,448
(Lifting easily)

485
00:20:58,248 --> 00:21:01,878
(Like a true teto-girl, she handles the heavy burner with ease.)

486
00:21:02,178 --> 00:21:03,378
(Wide apart)

487
00:21:03,378 --> 00:21:04,518
This isn't necessary.

488
00:21:04,518 --> 00:21:06,548
(She sets the burner down in a powerful stance.)

489
00:21:07,658 --> 00:21:10,618
(The bricks to protect against the heat are lined up perfectly.)

490
00:21:11,528 --> 00:21:12,588
This is exhausting.

491
00:21:12,928 --> 00:21:14,498
It must've been hard for You Seok.

492
00:21:16,098 --> 00:21:17,258
(Even when it gets tough,)

493
00:21:17,258 --> 00:21:20,628
(she never overlooks the little details.)

494
00:21:21,598 --> 00:21:24,108
(While Yoon Seo gets the burners ready)

495
00:21:25,368 --> 00:21:27,338
All right.

496
00:21:27,978 --> 00:21:29,608
I'll prepare the vegetables again.

497
00:21:29,608 --> 00:21:30,608
(Sun Young starts washing ingredients by the outdoor sink.)

498
00:21:30,608 --> 00:21:32,608
We won't eat a lot for breakfast.

499
00:21:32,608 --> 00:21:33,678
(She takes time to chat with the viewers.)

500
00:21:33,678 --> 00:21:34,848
So I'll wash three of them.

501
00:21:35,778 --> 00:21:37,318
Viewers, doesn't it look refreshing?

502
00:21:37,318 --> 00:21:40,518
It's best to wash it like giving a rinse on the neck.

503
00:21:40,648 --> 00:21:43,118
To remove all the pesticides, you must soak it...

504
00:21:43,118 --> 00:21:45,728
for about ten minutes. I told you yesterday.

505
00:21:45,728 --> 00:21:47,258
But we don't have enough time.

506
00:21:47,258 --> 00:21:49,128
You can just rinse it...

507
00:21:49,128 --> 00:21:50,198
(A handy washing tip when you're short on time)

508
00:21:50,198 --> 00:21:51,628
Under a strong stream of water.

509
00:21:52,168 --> 00:21:54,238
(Laughing)

510
00:21:54,798 --> 00:21:55,998
It's all washed.

511
00:21:56,838 --> 00:21:59,438
Next is mung bean sprouts.

512
00:21:59,438 --> 00:22:00,638
(It's time to wash mung bean sprouts next.)

513
00:22:00,738 --> 00:22:03,078
Jung Ah, do you need all these mung bean sprouts?

514
00:22:03,478 --> 00:22:04,508
No.

515
00:22:04,508 --> 00:22:06,448
Shouldn't I still rinse them all?

516
00:22:06,448 --> 00:22:07,748
- No.
- No?

517
00:22:07,748 --> 00:22:10,848
Just rinse enough for today's breakfast.

518
00:22:11,118 --> 00:22:13,388
Then I'll wash one-third of the bag.

519
00:22:14,858 --> 00:22:16,218
One-third of mung bean sprouts.

520
00:22:16,788 --> 00:22:17,828
About this much.

521
00:22:18,388 --> 00:22:20,328
Is it too much? Oh, no. It's too much.

522
00:22:21,128 --> 00:22:22,258
Mung bean sprouts...

523
00:22:22,258 --> 00:22:23,428
