2573
01:43:55,671 --> 01:43:56,811
- It's disappointing.
- In second place...

2574
01:43:56,811 --> 01:43:58,411
- I hope I'm in second place.
- But I didn't come in last.

2575
01:44:01,711 --> 01:44:03,181
A score of 78 points.

2576
01:44:03,481 --> 01:44:05,081
The score difference is only two.

2577
01:44:05,221 --> 01:44:06,321
Indian Matfia.

2578
01:44:06,321 --> 01:44:07,821
(Indian Matfia, a total of 78 points)

2579
01:44:07,821 --> 01:44:09,321
(Chef Yum: 43 points, Public panel: 35 points)

2580
01:44:11,191 --> 01:44:12,361
Hae Joon must've placed first.

2581
01:44:12,361 --> 01:44:14,131
- No, I don't think so.
- Or is it Sun Young?

2582
01:44:14,131 --> 01:44:15,291
(Plump Ravioli With Joons collapses with anxiety.)

2583
01:44:15,391 --> 01:44:18,401
(Curry Showdown's Current Ranking)

2584
01:44:18,401 --> 01:44:21,401
(2. Indian Matfia: 78, 3. Do You Know Hidden: 76)

2585
01:44:23,001 --> 01:44:24,841
Only the 1st and 4th place remain.

2586
01:44:25,201 --> 01:44:27,541
One of you placed first, and one of you placed last.

2587
01:44:28,671 --> 01:44:32,281
(Joons ran around tirelessly and gave his all.)

2588
01:44:33,051 --> 01:44:35,451
(Meanwhile, Auntie Curry aimed for bonus points.)

2589
01:44:36,151 --> 01:44:39,651
(But the unexpected taste left her feeling uneasy.)

2590
01:44:40,121 --> 01:44:42,961
The 1st place earned 79 points.

2591
01:44:44,391 --> 01:44:47,261
(Chef Yum's score 45 points versus 39 points)

2592
01:44:48,161 --> 01:44:53,771
(Who will be the winner of the curry showdown?)

2593
01:44:54,271 --> 01:44:56,701
In 1st place, Auntie Curry.

2594
01:44:56,701 --> 01:45:00,271
(Auntie Curry turns the tables.)

2595
01:45:01,511 --> 01:45:06,911
(Plump Ravioli With Joons places last.)

2596
01:45:07,851 --> 01:45:13,091
(My entire life as a chef is falling apart.)

2597
01:45:13,521 --> 01:45:15,951
(Plump Ravioli With Joons, a total of 69 points)

2598
01:45:15,951 --> 01:45:18,491
(Chef Yum: 45 points, Public panel: 24 points)

2599
01:45:18,521 --> 01:45:21,931
I just wanted to avoid coming in last.

2600
01:45:21,931 --> 01:45:23,331
(Public panel's verdict: The dumplings are salty.)

2601
01:45:23,331 --> 01:45:25,131
(It makes me crave more rice.)

2602
01:45:25,661 --> 01:45:28,371
(Auntie Curry, a total of 79 points)

2603
01:45:28,371 --> 01:45:30,701
(Chef Yum: 39 points, Public panel: 40 points)

2604
01:45:31,301 --> 01:45:32,441
(Public panel's verdict: It's smooth and familiar.)

2605
01:45:32,441 --> 01:45:33,541
(A perfect combination of apples and cheese)

2606
01:45:33,541 --> 01:45:35,641
This is unbelievable.

2607
01:45:35,641 --> 01:45:36,841
Thank you.

2608
01:45:38,011 --> 01:45:43,751
(An unexpected twist completely defied expectations.)

2609
01:45:43,751 --> 01:45:46,791
I will work even harder from now on.

2610
01:45:46,791 --> 01:45:47,891
(Sorrow, joy)

2611
01:45:47,891 --> 01:45:49,121
Seriously.

2612
01:45:49,361 --> 01:45:50,861
I can't believe it.

2613
01:45:51,391 --> 01:45:52,691
I got goosebumps on my face.

2614
01:45:52,731 --> 01:45:55,761
- That's so funny.
- I will never...

2615
01:45:56,501 --> 01:45:57,861
make curry in my life.

2616
01:45:57,861 --> 01:46:01,331
(His clothes and spirit are both in tatters.)

2617
01:46:02,101 --> 01:46:04,971
Isn't this wild rock seaweed that's known to be expensive?

2618
01:46:05,201 --> 01:46:07,341
- Thank you so much.
- I'm so jealous.

2619
01:46:07,341 --> 01:46:08,911
How much would that cost?

2620
01:46:08,911 --> 01:46:10,441
It's what we harvested.

2621
01:46:11,141 --> 01:46:12,481
- Thank you.
- Congratulations.

2622
01:46:12,481 --> 01:46:13,581
(A meaningful Fresh off the Sea gift)

2623
01:46:13,581 --> 01:46:14,681
Congratulations.

2624
01:46:15,111 --> 01:46:17,351
- Let's eat.
- Let me try the number one curry.

2625
01:46:19,251 --> 01:46:22,151
Everyone, this is the number one curry.

2626
01:46:22,151 --> 01:46:23,991
Please give it a try.

2627
01:46:24,921 --> 01:46:26,931
You gave me a lot of rice.

2628
01:46:26,931 --> 01:46:27,991
There's no kimchi.

2629
01:46:27,991 --> 01:46:29,031
(Everyone shares Auntie Curry's 1st-place curry.)

2630
01:46:29,031 --> 01:46:30,101
It's delicious.

2631
01:46:30,701 --> 01:46:32,631
- You could've placed 2nd.
- I should've placed 2nd.

2632
01:46:33,801 --> 01:46:34,831
(Humming)

2633
01:46:34,831 --> 01:46:36,601
The savoury flavour of the cheese...

2634
01:46:37,271 --> 01:46:38,701
captivated many people.

2635
01:46:39,171 --> 01:46:40,171
It's good.

2636
01:46:40,171 --> 01:46:41,241
(A curry worthy of taking first place)

2637
01:46:41,241 --> 01:46:43,181
Mine is my favourite.

2638
01:46:44,281 --> 01:46:46,651
What caused the failure? Is it the dumpling?

2639
01:46:46,651 --> 01:46:48,151
(One man is still trying to figure out what went wrong.)

2640
01:46:48,851 --> 01:46:49,981
Mine has...

2641
01:46:50,481 --> 01:46:51,951
a horrible aftertaste.

2642
01:46:53,121 --> 01:46:57,221
(Laughing)

2643
01:46:57,861 --> 01:46:59,561
The dumpling flavour is way too strong.

2644
01:46:59,561 --> 01:47:02,431
- It overpowers everything.
- That's important.

2645
01:47:03,201 --> 01:47:04,761
The dumplings take over the whole dish.

2646
01:47:04,761 --> 01:47:05,831
(Listen carefully and take notes)

2647
01:47:05,831 --> 01:47:07,331
My favourite is Hae Joon's.

2648
01:47:07,471 --> 01:47:08,501
(Shocked)

2649
01:47:08,501 --> 01:47:10,641
For me, it had the lightest taste.

2650
01:47:11,171 --> 01:47:13,171
(Feeling bitter)

2651
01:47:14,441 --> 01:47:17,011
(Let's see.)

2652
01:47:17,311 --> 01:47:20,481
(Sun Young serves 3 different curries in 1 bowl.)

2653
01:47:24,621 --> 01:47:25,651
It's incredible.

2654
01:47:26,121 --> 01:47:27,991
(What is it?)

2655
01:47:27,991 --> 01:47:30,621
It tastes the best when the three are mixed together.

2656
01:47:30,961 --> 01:47:32,161
Except Hae Joon's.

2657
01:47:35,591 --> 01:47:37,661
It's just like Fresh off the Sea.

2658
01:47:37,831 --> 01:47:39,631
When we're alone, we may not shine,

2659
01:47:39,631 --> 01:47:40,901
