2697
01:49:02,281 --> 01:49:03,881
(Do we have a guest today?)

2698
01:49:03,981 --> 01:49:06,021
(A rocker?)

2699
01:49:06,291 --> 01:49:08,891
(A rocker is coming to Fresh off the Sea?)

2700
01:49:10,861 --> 01:49:11,961
(The second guest, Cho Jung Seok)

2701
01:49:12,321 --> 01:49:13,331
(Screaming)

2702
01:49:18,361 --> 01:49:21,301
(Screaming)

2703
01:49:22,201 --> 01:49:25,141
(It's hard to believe that Cho Jung Seok is on this show!)

2704
01:49:26,141 --> 01:49:27,971
(This vast, wide-open place is...)

2705
01:49:28,741 --> 01:49:30,481
(Taean, South Chungcheong Province, with rich mudflat resources)

2706
01:49:30,481 --> 01:49:31,881
(Manila clams are pure rock too!)

2707
01:49:31,881 --> 01:49:33,551
(The Siblings' Manila Clam Festival will take place.)

2708
01:49:34,051 --> 01:49:37,181
(The siblings made their debut as Manila clam rockers.)

2709
01:49:37,681 --> 01:49:39,081
(They can't stop shaking it.)

2710
01:49:39,351 --> 01:49:41,591
(Manila clams are pure rock too.)

2711
01:49:41,591 --> 01:49:43,361
(Manila clams are pure joy?)

2712
01:49:43,821 --> 01:49:45,361
(The guest singer on the show, Cho Jung Seok)

2713
01:49:45,361 --> 01:49:46,491
(Jung Ja, Jung Seok's alter ego on Fresh off the Sea)

2714
01:49:46,761 --> 01:49:48,531
(When an older member sings,)

2715
01:49:48,531 --> 01:49:50,131
(the youngest member sings along.)

2716
01:49:50,431 --> 01:49:52,561
(When the oldest member starts a role play,)

2717
01:49:52,931 --> 01:49:54,801
(the guest plays along with her.)

2718
01:49:54,901 --> 01:49:58,241
(They can't stop laughing, thanks to Jung Seok.)

2719
01:49:58,401 --> 01:50:00,241
(Everyone falls for Jung Seok, the lucky charm.)

2720
01:50:02,041 --> 01:50:03,711
(They fall into the mud too.)

2721
01:50:04,341 --> 01:50:06,611
